plugin-qualify (0.20.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * descriptors test: the fixture bundles are 27 since the instrument
    fixtures joined the eq10q ones
  * commit-msg: the hook is the shared stub again, byte for byte
  * tests: refusal-codes reads a placeholder name the type checker can prove
    is a string (#27)
  * scan: a toggle named bypass means bypass; a duplicate port symbol refuses
    the plugin (#27)
  * tests: EQ10Q-shaped fixtures for a bypass toggle and a duplicate port
    symbol, red (#27)
  * pool step test: the sweep over the two synth fixtures times one point of
    the voice curve
  * qualify: every process that loads a plugin starts with a HOME of the
    run's own
  * clap-qualify: the voice curve, timed with every parameter at its default
  * lv2-measure: the voice curve is timed with every parameter at its default
  * lv2-measure: an instrument's audio inputs carry silence in the cost pass
  * lv2-measure: an instrument with an audio input is played, by its class
    lv2:InstrumentPlugin
  * docs: an LV2 instrument's probe count, its curve of notes, its settle and
    its silence
  * lv2-measure: an instrument that sounded and died away is timed; only one
    that never sounded is silent
  * qualify: an LV2 instrument is timed at the declared curve of notes, and
    the record keeps it
  * lv2-measure: an instrument is given time to build its sound, timed
    sounding, and timed at each count of notes
  * qualify: an LV2 instrument is played with the declared count of notes held
  * qualify: the console is judged at 96000/256, and 96000/1024 stays a
    measured cell (#19)
  * Name Open-Mixer and OpenMixer, not FreeMixer, in the manual page, the
    docs and the CLAP host
  * tests: the sweep's sync runs take their directories from a plugin-hostd
    --search-path stand-in
  * Release 0.20.3
  * packaging: the path unit's folders and the installed check from
    plugin-hostd --search-path
  * sync: the directories scanned are the ones plugin-hostd --search-path
    prints
  * packaging: the package metadata names the Open-Mixer repository

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:02:55 +0000
